ool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "Interesting! After pressing SPACE, the blue block reset to cols 12-31, not cols 24-43 as I expected. So SPACE does reset the blue block position, but only when the game is over. When the game is still running, SPACE just restarts the timer without resetting the position.\nAlso, I notice the yellow structures have a more complex shape. Looking at the boundary:\n- Left yellow: [[52, 16], [52, 19], [55, 19], [56, 20], [56, 23], [55, 24], [52, 24], [52, 27], [59, 27], [59, 16]]\nThis describes a shape that has a gap in the middle. Let me visualize it:\n- Rows 52-55: cols 16-19 and cols 24-27 (two 4x4 blocks)\n- Rows 56-59: cols 16-27 (one 4x12 block)\nSo the left yellow structure has a gap at rows 56-59, cols 20-23. Wait, that doesn't match the boundary.\nLet me re-read the boundary: [[52, 16], [52, 19], [55, 19], [56, 20], [56, 23], [55, 24], [52, 24], [52, 27], [59, 27], [59, 16]]\nThis is a clockwise perimeter. Let me trace it:\n- [52, 16] to [52, 19]: top edge, cols 16-19\n- [52, 19] to [55, 19]: right edge of left part, rows 52-55\n- [55, 19] to [56, 20]: diagonal down-right\n- [56, 20] to [56, 23]: bottom edge of gap, cols 20-23\n- [56, 23] to [55, 24]: diagonal up-right\n- [55, 24] to [52, 24]: left edge of right part, rows 52-55\n- [52, 24] to [52, 27]: top edge, cols 24-27\n- [52, 27] to [59, 27]: right edge, rows 52-59\n- [59, 27] to [59, 16]: bottom edge, cols 16-27\n- [59, 16] to [52, 16]: left edge, rows 52-59\nSo the shape is:\n- Rows 52-55: cols 16-19 and cols 24-27 (two 4x4 blocks with a gap at cols 20-23)\n- Rows 56-59: cols 16-27 (one 4x12 block)\nWait, that doesn't make sense. Let me re-trace:\n- [52, 16] to [52, 19]: top edge of left block, cols 16-19\n- [52, 19] to [55, 19]: right edge of left block, rows 52-55\n- [55, 19] to [56, 20]: diagonal down-right (corner)\n- [56, 20] to [56, 23]: bottom edge of gap, cols 20-23\n- [56, 23] to [55, 24]: diagonal up-right (corner)\n- [55, 24] to [52, 